# The Repository menu of every tool (README, Version control): what a folder offers depends on
# the marker its own tool left in it and on what that tool can do (the capability table). The
# folders are marker fixtures — `.git` with its HEAD, `.hg`, `.svn`, `CVS/Repository`,
# `vssver2.scc` — because the menu reads nothing else; what each client answers is measured in
# tests/vcs_backends.rs.

# Off until switched on: no version-control items anywhere.
open $T/plain
expect-no-menu-item Repository
open $T/gitcopy
expect-no-menu-item Repository
action app.vcs-integration

# A folder no tool owns: Repository with Clone and Create repository here.
open $T/plain
expect-menu-item Repository
expect-menu-item Clone...
expect-menu-item Create repository here...
expect-no-menu-item Show log

# Git: Sync and Commit at the top, the distributed items in the submenu, no central Update, no
# locks, nothing to clone into a folder Git already owns.
open $T/gitcopy
expect-menu-item Git Sync...
expect-menu-item Git Commit -> "main"...
expect-menu-item Pull...
expect-menu-item Fetch...
expect-menu-item Push...
expect-menu-item Show log
expect-menu-item Show Reflog
expect-menu-item Check for modifications
expect-menu-item Stash Save
expect-menu-item Clean up...
expect-menu-item Merge...
expect-menu-item Create Branch...
expect-menu-item Export...
expect-menu-item Create Patch Serial...
expect-menu-item Apply Patch Serial...
expect-menu-item Settings
expect-no-menu-item Git Update
expect-no-menu-item Get Lock...
expect-no-menu-item Clone...

# Mercurial: distributed as well, with its own branch name; no reflog.
open $T/hgcopy
expect-menu-item Hg Sync...
expect-menu-item Hg Commit -> "default"...
expect-menu-item Pull...
expect-menu-item Push...
expect-menu-item Stash Save
expect-menu-item Clean up...
expect-no-menu-item Show Reflog
expect-no-menu-item Hg Update

# Subversion: a central store updates instead of pulling, and has nothing of its own to push.
open $T/svncopy
expect-menu-item SVN Update
expect-menu-item Clean up...
expect-menu-item Merge...
expect-menu-item Apply Patch Serial...
expect-no-menu-item SVN Sync...
expect-no-menu-item Pull...
expect-no-menu-item Push...
expect-no-menu-item Fetch...
expect-no-menu-item Stash Save
expect-no-menu-item Show Reflog

# CVS: no rename, no patch of its own, no clean-up; its branch is its sticky tag, HEAD without one.
open $T/cvs
expect-menu-item CVS Update
expect-menu-item CVS Commit -> "HEAD"...
expect-menu-item Create Branch...
expect-menu-item Create Patch Serial...
expect-no-menu-item Apply Patch Serial...
expect-no-menu-item Clean up...
expect-no-menu-item Push...

# Visual Source Safe: no merge, no branches, no blame, no ignore list, no patches.
open $T/vsscopy
expect-menu-item VSS Update
expect-menu-item Check for modifications
expect-no-menu-item Merge...
expect-no-menu-item Create Branch...
expect-no-menu-item Export...
expect-no-menu-item Create Patch Serial...
expect-no-menu-item Clean up...

# A folder that only holds a working copy deeper down is not one: Clone stays; the folder the
# marker sits in is the working copy, and so is a folder below it.
open $T/wrapper
expect-menu-item Clone...
expect-no-menu-item Git Commit -> "main"...
open $T/wrapper/inner
expect-menu-item Git Commit -> "main"...
open $T/gitcopy/deep
expect-menu-item Git Commit -> "main"...
expect-no-menu-item Clone...
